-- Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 - its bestiary and its notable NPCs.
-- 0 creatures (migration 074) and 3 notable NPCs (migration 072),
-- with their attacks in stat_attacks (migration 073).
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-triax-2-bestiary.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/bestiary-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every
-- creature row passes creatureFormulaGaps, every value is printable ASCII,
-- and an 8-word shingle check of the prose fields against the book's cached text finds no copied run.

INSERT INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES
('jinna-gir-song', 'Jinna Gir Song', NULL, 'Leader of the Song Warriors', 'rifts', 'Adult Chiang-Ku Dragon', '11th level Chiang Ku Dragon R.C.C.', 11, 'Scrupulous', NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"IQ":22,"ME":24,"MA":24,"PS":25,"PP":17,"PE":16,"PB":17,"Spd":22}', NULL, NULL, 1000, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'P.S. 25 is Supernatural. M.D.C. 1,000, and 1,000 more while she is in her natural dragon form. The book gives Quick Stats only: no combat bonuses, attacks per melee, skills, spells or powers are printed; it points to Rifts World Book 3: England for the Chiang-Ku Dragon R.C.C.', NULL, NULL, 'Those of an adult Chiang-Ku Dragon (Rifts World Book 3: England). She normally goes about in a form other than her dragon one, which is why her M.D.C. doubles when she reverts.', 'A master of Tattoo Magic - rumour has it her forebears helped invent the art. Her own body carries many Magic Tattoos, some extremely rare and a few unknown on Earth for thousands of years, and she has tattooed many of her followers, including with rare and forgotten designs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'She and her fighters keep hidden supply caches and arms depots across Italy, France, Switzerland, Austria and Germany. She rewards fighters of outstanding courage and skill with magic tattoos, magic items or high-tech weapons.', NULL, 'A centuries-old foe of the Splugorth whose hatred of them and of their Gargoyle troops is personal. She prefers to stay clear of other peoples'' politics and to help from the shadows rather than openly, trusting that her aid is valued even when unacknowledged.', 'The Song Warriors: about 1,500 fighters recruited by invitation from across the Megaverse and split into cells of 100-200 working in France, Switzerland, Austria, Germany and northwestern Italy, sometimes Belgium, Spain and England. Roughly 50% True Atlanteans, 20% humans, 10% Elves and Dwarves, 5% dragons (she is the only Chiang-Ku), 5% good-aligned Ogres, Trolls and similar races, 5% Psi-Stalkers and Simvan, 5% others; about a fifth are escapees from Atlantean slavery with no training to speak of (equal to the Vagabond O.C.C.). Common O.C.C.s include Atlantean Undead Slayers, Tattooed Masters and Monster Hunters, Mercenary Soldiers, Combat Cyborgs, Juicers, Crazies, Ley Line Walkers, Shifters, Druids, Wilderness Scouts, Operators, Body Fixers and former NGR soldiers. Their human members buy energy weapons, ammunition and explosives from Triax, mercenaries, adventurers or wilderness folk (never the Black Market) and salvage Splugorth, Kittani and Gargoyle gear; power armor and vehicles are scarce and mostly light, fast Triax types such as the Terrain Hopper and Predator. Has fought beside General Rasheen several times, though not since he entered NGR office. Covertly feeds intelligence to the NGR military.', 'The Splugorth of Atlantis and their Minions, the Gargoyle Empire, Kittani warriors and slavers', 'An adult Chiang-Ku Dragon who leads a resistance band of humans, D-Bees and True Atlanteans against the Gargoyles and the Splugorth. Moved by the Gargoyle Retribution of 38 P.A., she chose to help the human-supremacist NGR covertly rather than approach it, running a guerilla war of infiltration, scouting and supply-line raids that keeps Atlantean weapons and power armor out of Gargoyle hands. NGR scouts in southern France confirmed her existence in August 105 P.A., partly through the Gargoyles'' own complaints about her. She spent 104 to mid-107 P.A. fighting the Minions of Splugorth and helping locals, and was pivotal in Operation Sea Storm in 107 P.A. Her entry builds on the one in Rifts World Book 3: England (p.48).', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.17-18'),
('struwwelpeter', 'Struwwelpeter', NULL, 'Dream Peter', 'rifts', 'Unknown Greater Supernatural Being; possibly one of a kind, or an ancient Chaos Demon Lord', 'Equal to a 12th level Assassin and Mystic', 12, 'Diabolic', 'Unknown; presumed immortal', '11 feet, 3 inches (3.4 m)', '250 lbs (112.5 kg)', '{"IQ":14,"ME":21,"MA":24,"PS":20,"PP":22,"PE":18,"PB":8,"Spd":25}', 60, 28, 160, 600, 160, 10, 15, '{"attacks":6,"strike":4,"parry":4,"dodge":7,"disarm":1,"pull":4,"roll":4}', 'Attribute bonuses included. +11 to strike or parry when using his fingernail claws/blades (the +4 is otherwise). +6% save vs coma/death, +2 save vs magic, +3 save vs psionic attacks, Critical Strike on a 19 or 20. P.S. 20 is Supernatural, so his blows do M.D. Mega-Damage 160; the 60 Hit Points, 28 S.D.C. and A.R. 10 apply in S.D.C. environments. Horror Factor 15 to people of the Black Forest, 12 elsewhere; in dreams his Awe Factor runs 8-15 and in nightmares 12-15. Only two attacks per melee while in the dream world.', '[{"name":"Creative Writing","pct":80},{"name":"Performance","pct":85},{"name":"Sing","pct":80},{"name":"Cook","pct":60},{"name":"Dance","pct":98},{"name":"Play Musical Instrument: Piano","pct":80},{"name":"Play Musical Instrument: Violin","pct":80},{"name":"Play Musical Instrument: Fiddle","pct":80},{"name":"Play Musical Instrument: Flute","pct":80},{"name":"Play Musical Instrument: Guitar","pct":80},{"name":"Play Musical Instrument: Accordion","pct":80},{"name":"Sewing","pct":90},{"name":"Impersonation","pct":90},{"name":"Tracking","pct":90},{"name":"Juggling","pct":70},{"name":"Prowl","pct":70},{"name":"Imitate Voices and Sounds","pct":60},{"name":"Tailing","pct":90},{"name":"Art","pct":95}]', 'W.P. Knife, W.P. Sword and Paired Weapons, all at 12th level. The book prints the six instruments as one Play Musical Instruments entry at 80%.', 'Magically speaks and reads every language; sees the invisible, has sharp ordinary sight plus nightvision to 200 feet (61 m), turns invisible at will (must become visible to attack); Bio-Regenerates 1D6 M.D.C. per melee round. Claws: his fingernails can shrink to two inches (5 cm) or grow to two feet (0.6 m), always inflicting M.D., and can fuse into a single wide scythe-like blade; used as daggers, short swords or shears to lop off appendages, and as torture tools. Metamorphosis: an impish boy of 14-16, a hunchbacked old man, a well-dressed gentleman or a big shaggy dog; as the dog he has Spd 45 (30 mph/48 km) and a bite of 4D6 S.D.C. (2D4 M.D. against Mega-Damage foes) whose victim must save vs disease or fall feverish for 1D6 days with attacks per melee halved, P.E. down 70%, a -4 penalty on every combat action, no initiative at all and -25% on skills. Dimensional Teleport at 80%, but only to the plane of dreams, from which he can reach mortal worlds and drift between the minds of sleepers, daydreamers and the creatively absorbed; sub-demons are as easy to enter, but magical creatures and lesser supernaturals save at +4, Greater Demons and greater supernatural beings at +7, Demon Lords and gods at +12, and they must be in the mortal realm. In the dream world he cannot touch the physical world and knows of it only what dreams tell him. If slain in the physical world he is cast unconscious into the dream world and returns in 2D6 years. Vulnerabilities: magic and psionics affect him fully; like Faerie Folk he cannot cross salt, so an unbroken salt circle traps him, a salt line halts him and a salt-ringed bed bars him from the sleeper''s dreams, and he cannot clear the salt himself; he bores quickly and can juggle only one or two schemes at once; he is frustrated by those who refuse his games and works to draw them in rather than harming them; he leaves Principled characters alone unless they provoke him.', '600 P.P.E.; casts as a 12th level Mystic. Spells limited to: Apparition, Armor Bizarre, Befuddle, Charismatic Aura, Charm, Compulsion, Distant Voice, Fear, Fly as the Eagle, Fool''s Gold, Heavy Breathing, Horror, Impervious to Energy, Locate, Luck Curse, Magic Net, Mask of Deceit, Multiple Image, Reduce Self, Shadow Meld, Speed of the Snail, Wall of the Weird, Wisps of Confusion and World Bizarre.', '160 I.S.P.; a Master Psionic equal to a 12th level Mystic. Powers limited to: Alter Aura, Astral Projection, Deaden Senses, Empathy, Empathic Transmission, Hypnotic Suggestion, Induce Sleep, Object Read, Mentally Possess Others, Mind Block, Mind Bond, Psychic Omni-Sight, Radiate Horror Factor, Remote Viewing, See Aura, Sixth Sense and Telepathy.', NULL, 'None; his supernatural body rejects implants', 'None; he uses no weapon or device of any kind and relies on his own powers', NULL, 'Theatrical to the core: big hand gestures, a face that runs through every emotion, talk full of metaphor, limericks and rhyme. He likes a flamboyant kill, keeping victims alive for the drama and sometimes closing with a little poem or moral about how they earned their fate. That showmanship makes him linger too long, leave captives where they can be rescued and take silly risks, and his total self-confidence leads him to badly underrate opponents and the pawns he plays with.', 'None he counts as true allies; every living thing, Demon Lords and gods included, is a toy to him. He gets on well with evil, ugly Faerie Folk, who find him great fun and may help, hide, trade or party with him. He is presently using the Gargoyles as game pieces, apparently to raise a rival Gargoyle Empire against Zerstrun''s, and has grown fond of them the way a puppeteer is of puppets.', 'Emperor Zerstrun is his rival in the current game. He regards all living beings as playthings, holds the Black Forest''s humans and D-Bees, and thinking creatures generally, in contempt.', 'Pronounced STRU-vel-PAY-ter and called Dream Peter, Shaggy Peter or Shock-Haired Peter: an evil supernatural being of the Black Forest who lives in both the physical world and the realm of dreams, sowing nightmares and tragedy. Once a pre-Rifts fairy tale, he crossed into the physical world with the Cataclysm, and his favourite shape is a towering, gangly youth of about 13-15 with wild hair, a crooked grin, a hooked nose and foot-long claw-nails, who prances through the woods to music only he hears. Most NGR soldiers and Polizei dismiss him as folklore - only about 20% believe he is real - yet he planted the dream of empire in Zerstrun, pushed resentful D-Bees to murder the NGR President, set Gargoyle lords against their Emperor and urged the Brodkil on to Wroclaw. He now works through the dreams of Gargoyle leaders in the western half of the split Empire, and a few thousand Gargoyles around the Black Forest are wholly his.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.30-32'),
('general-rasheen', 'General Rasheen', NULL, 'General of the NGR Army and member of the Council of Governors', 'rifts', 'Four-armed giant D-Bee from another world (born on Earth near Amsterdam)', '10th level Cyber-Knight', 10, 'Principled', 'About 120', '16 feet (4.8 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":11,"ME":14,"MA":14,"PS":30,"PP":14,"PE":18,"PB":14,"Spd":15}', NULL, NULL, 268, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'P.S. 30 is Supernatural. M.D.C. 268 is his own body; his Cyber-Knight Cyber-Armor adds 98 M.D.C. at A.R. 17. Quick Stats only: no combat bonuses, attacks per melee or psionics are printed.', '[{"name":"Language and Literacy: Euro","pct":80},{"name":"Language and Literacy: American","pct":80},{"name":"Language and Literacy: Dragonese/Elven","pct":80},{"name":"Language and Literacy: Gobblely","pct":80},{"name":"Language and Literacy: Spanish","pct":80},{"name":"Language and Literacy: Pre-Rifts German","pct":80},{"name":"Language and Literacy: Pre-Rifts French","pct":80},{"name":"Public Speaking","pct":60},{"name":"Creative Writing","pct":45},{"name":"Law (NGR-specific)","pct":55},{"name":"Philosophy","pct":75},{"name":"Research","pct":50},{"name":"Military Etiquette","pct":95},{"name":"Horsemanship: Cyber-Knight","pct":98}]', 'Horsemanship: Cyber-Knight is printed 98%/80%; the first figure is stored. The seven languages are printed as one list, spoken and read at 80%. Paired Weapons; W.P. Sword, Energy Rifle, Energy Pistol, Heavy M.D. Weapons, Archery, Targeting, Spear, Axe and Blunt, all at 10th level.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'One bionic replacement arm (his lower left), robotic P.S. 30, with a particle beam cannon built into the palm', 'Cyber-Knight Cyber-Armor (98 M.D.C., A.R. 17); palm particle beam cannon in his bionic arm (damage not given in the Quick Stats)', NULL, 'Warm, honest and plain-spoken, a gentle giant off the battlefield who argues for D-Bee equality by making people confront that he is one. He is no politician but speaks well, and his sincerity is hard to argue with. Privately he is growing frustrated with the Council of Governors and fears he has given the NGR''s D-Bees false hope, though he treats this as one more hard fight he means to win.', 'President Viktoria Sperling, who also works to improve conditions for D-Bees; the Order of Cyber-Knights; the NGR Army and the human and D-Bee soldiers who have served under him; Jinna Gir Song, beside whom he fought several times before entering office', 'The Gargoyle Empire and the Brodkil; the well-funded anti-D-Bee lobby and the politicians who back it', 'Born about 120 years ago in a D-Bee village near Amsterdam to a long-lived race of four-armed giants who prize courage and strength, Rasheen was raised as a warrior and defender. He left for North America as a mercenary around Lazlo and New Lazlo, where his mercy toward Coalition troops in a standoff at a Pennsylvania D-Bee village drew the Cyber-Knights to recruit him, and Sir Rasheen became a legend in the Order. Around 70 P.A. he came home to find Amsterdam taken by Gargoyles and waged a private war that earned him the name Giant Avenger and a following of humans and D-Bees, about 60% of them human. Public pressure eventually made the NGR enlist him, first to guard D-Bee border towns and then as a full Army officer; he is now the NGR''s most beloved war hero, plans campaigns that hold tens of thousands of lives, sits on the Council of Governors as the leading voice for D-Bee rights, and yet as a D-Bee cannot vote for President and has his other votes counted as half. Introduced through a Volkstimme Magazine interview by Gerfried Baum.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.65-68');

